From 0d946b9243bd247cc1db0a5bf23bc9c2a80fb882 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiago Leal <183942127+tiagonleal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:45:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Title textures: uploads start from the state the title's
 transitions left (#104 item 2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A texture kept in step with title memory was uploaded again with
barriers from (and back to) the state it was created in. Once the title
had moved it (COMMON -> PIXEL_SHADER_RESOURCE, one mip to COPY_SOURCE…)
the upload's "before" state was wrong; the D3D12 debug layer reports
exactly that (before state 0xC0 of subresource 1 does not match 0x800).

The title's transitions of these textures are noted per PC command list
as they are recorded (ResourceBarrier, console lists' replay at Close)
and applied to the texture's state when the list is submitted
(ExecuteCommandLists, KickoffX), in submission order and each time a
closed list runs; Reset / create / release forget a list's notes. The
state is kept per subresource while they differ, and the upload's
barriers follow it (texture::record_upload_states).

Tests: title_textures unit tests (state per subresource; notes apply on
submit, in order, again on re-submit, not after Reset), and
tests/texture_states.rs (own process, D3D12 debug layer): per-subresource
states give no error, the creation state for all gives the mismatch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c8d9549c8820edfe913555d31d2fc287c29fa786)
